Add Zebra ZP 450 driver entries

The ZP 450 is a rebadged Zebra GK420d: 203dpi, 4-inch, direct thermal.
Base units ship with EPL2 firmware; dual-firmware units also speak ZPL II.
Upstream LPrint has no ZP 450 entry, and its generic ZPL drivers carry empty
device IDs, so a ZPL ZP 450 matches no driver at all during auto-detection.

Real hardware (macOS 26, Mac Studio) reports its model as "ZTC ZP 450-200dpi",
which is what the primary entries match; the "_alt" entries cover units that
report the shorter "ZTC ZP 450". Matching is all-or-nothing per key, so a unit
reporting some other string simply falls through to the previous behavior.

